\cf3 U.S. Army {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Specialist_(rank)#Specialist_(1955%E2%80%93present)"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 Specialist 5}} (SP5) Tulsa McLean ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elvis_Presley"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 Elvis Presley}}) is a tank crewman with a singing career. Serving with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/3rd_Armored_Division_(United_States)"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 3rd Armored "Spearhead" Division}} in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Germany"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 West Germany}}, McLean dreams of running his own nightclub when he leaves the army, but such dreams don't come cheap. Tulsa and his buddies have formed a band and perform in various German "{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gasthaus"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 Gasthauses}}", nightclubs, and on an Armed Forces stage. In one bar, he even discovers the record "{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Suede_Shoes#Presley.27s_RCA_cover"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 Blue Suede Shoes}}" sung by someone named Elvis Presley on a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jukebox"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 jukebox}}.\cb1 \
\cb4 To raise money, Tulsa places a bet with his friend Dynamite ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edson_Stroll"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 Edson Stroll}}) that he can spend the night with a club dancer named Lili ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juliet_Prowse"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 Juliet Prowse}}), who is rumored to be hard to get since she turned down one other G.I. operator, Turk ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeremy_Slate"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 Jeremy Slate}}). Dynamite and Turk have vied for women before when the two were stationed in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hawaii"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 Hawaii}}. When Dynamite gets transferred to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alaska"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 Alaska}}, Tulsa is brought in to take his place. He is not looking forward to it, but must go through with it.\cb1 \
\cb4 Tulsa uses his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southern_United_States"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 Southern}} charm and calls Lili "ma'am." She at first sees Tulsa as another Occupation Duty GI. Then after a day on the Rhine, Lili begins to fall for him. Tulsa's friend Cookie, meanwhile, falls in love with Lili's roommate, Tina (Let\'edcia Rom\'e1n) from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Italy"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 Italy}}. In the end, Rick's and Marla's baby son Tiger helps Tulsa win the bet for the outfit\'97and Lili's heart.}